  "findings": "Compared the low rhizomatous flowering carpet and divided leaf photographs with revised seeds 1/4/7 and all 36 sheet entries. Dedicated architecture now separates three to five shoots along ground-level rhizomes; each has a three-part whorl of divided foliage below one white flower, replacing a generic five-leaf rosette. The generator places six petal segments but 25 mm rasterization reduces the 3-5 cm flowers to one or a few white cells. Height range approximately 0.12-0.25 m. Serrations and petal separation are below the chosen pitch; accepted as a scale-correct stylized spring carpet, with the fruit photograph used only to distinguish excluded post-flowering structure.",
